Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/eulerianCircuit()":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/euleriancircuit()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An Eulerian circuit by Hierholzer’s algorithm (Hierholzer and Wiener 1873), from the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order with an edge; nil when the graph is not Eulerian or has no edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Circuit"},{"text":" has at least one). Pinned: from the current vertex the first unused edge in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"text":" order, in the stack form igraph’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igraph_eulerian_cycle"},{"text":" runs; the circuit is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listed forward from that vertex. On a compressed sparse row the graph’s own rows are read.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"eulerianCircuit"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks7CircuitV","text":"Circuit"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"type":"topic","title":"eulerianCircuit()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/eulerianCircuit()"},"doc://Tou